00:21:00,200 --> 00:21:04,960
waves. Lake Ontario is the smallest of the Great Lakes.

237
00:21:05,460 --> 00:21:10,600
But compared with the others, Ontario is more elusive because of the Niagara Falls

238
00:21:10,600 --> 00:21:12,820
and its sheer thunderous drop.

239
00:21:13,600 --> 00:21:19,000
Lake Erie is the fourth largest lake by surface area of the five Great Lakes in

240
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:25,140
North America and the 13th largest globally if measured in terms of surface area.

241
00:21:25,700 --> 00:21:31,520
It is the southernmost, shallowest, and smallest by volume of the Great Lakes and

242
00:21:31,520 --> 00:21:35,560
therefore also has the shortest average water residence time.

243
00:21:36,860 --> 00:21:40,080
Lake Huron is the second largest of the lakes.

244
00:21:40,840 --> 00:21:45,900
It is shared on the east by the Canadian province of Ontario and on the west by the

245
00:21:45,900 --> 00:21:48,400
state of Michigan in the United States.

246
00:21:49,100 --> 00:21:53,620
The name of the lake is derived from early French explorers who named it for the

247
00:21:53,620 --> 00:21:55,640
Huron people inhabiting the region.

248
00:21:57,500 --> 00:22:02,960
The Huronian glaciation was named due to evidence collected from Lake Huron region.

249
00:22:02,960 --> 00:22:08,960
Lake Michigan is the only one of the five Great Lakes of North America that is

250
00:22:08,960 --> 00:22:12,140
located entirely within the United States.

251
00:22:12,540 --> 00:22:18,280
Lake Michigan is shared from west to east by the US states of Wisconsin, Illinois,

252
00:22:18,760 --> 00:22:20,420
Indiana, and Michigan.

253
00:22:21,260 --> 00:22:27,060
The word Michigan originally referred to the lake itself and is believed to come

254
00:22:27,060 --> 00:22:30,980
from the Ojibwa word michigami, meaning great water.

255
00:22:30,980 --> 00:22:37,500
Our destination now is Superior, the largest freshwater lake in the world, also the

256
00:22:37,500 --> 00:22:39,340
deepest one of the five Great Lakes.

257
00:22:40,160 --> 00:22:44,460
If you stood on the moon, you could see the Great Lakes and recognize the familiar

258
00:22:44,460 --> 00:22:46,440
wolf head shape of Lake Superior.

259
00:22:47,160 --> 00:22:49,880
There is a graceful stillness on Lake Superior.

260
00:22:50,300 --> 00:22:55,140
The rounded humped along the shores look like burial mounds of the gods.

261
00:22:55,680 --> 00:22:59,520
Yet for all their size and power, the Great Lakes are fragile.

262
00:22:59,520 --> 00:23:05,460
In the past, this fragile nature wasn't recognized and the lakes were mistreated for

263
00:23:05,460 --> 00:23:11,180
economic gain, placing the ecosystem under tremendous stress from human activities.

